<title>BELGIUM: KB SEES ONLY TWO OUTPERFORMERS ON BRUSSELS BOURSE.</title>
<headline>KB SEES ONLY TWO OUTPERFORMERS ON BRUSSELS BOURSE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank Kredietbank said in its August summary on the Brussels share market it was neutral plus or neutral minus on most issues.</p>
<p>Only two out of 75 issues were rated market outperformers: computer software company Real Software and packaged meats and foods company Ter Beke . The recommendations were based on stock prices on August 1 of respectively 2,600 and 3,400 Belgian francs.</p>
<p>KB rates a stock a market outperformer when it expects it will outperform the Bel-20 blue chip index by more than 10 percent over the next 12-18 months.</p>
<p>KB rated the following as market underperformers: hotel and airline group City Hotels (4,850 francs), shipper CMB (2,500 francs), construction firm Franki (495 francs), mineral water group Spadel (40,500 francs), tour operator Sun International (3,250 francs) and fun park operator Walibi (1,270 francs).</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
